{
  "title": "Aamaal of Zohr Prayers on Friday",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Twenty-First: Among the recommended acts on Fridays is that one may say the following supplicatory prayer at midday (zohr) as is narrated by Muhammad ibn Muslim on the authority of Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq, peace be upon him. Yet, the following form of the supplication has been quoted from Shaykh al-Tusi’s famous book entitled Misbah al-Mutahajjid:\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO\nThere is no god save Allah.\nوَ اللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nWAL LAAHO AKBARO\nAllah is the Most Great.\nوَ سُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ\nWA SUBHAANAL LAAHE\nGlory be to Allah.\nوَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ لَمْ يَتَّخِذْ وَلَدًا\nWAL HAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE LAM YATTAKHIZ WALADAN\nAll praise be to Allah Who has not taken to Himself a son \nوَ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ شَرِيْكٌ فِي الْمُلْكِ\nWA LAM YAKUN LAHU SHAREEKUN FIL MULKE\nnor has He had any partner in sovereignty\nوَ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ وَلِيٌّ مِنَ الذُّلِّ\nWA LAM YAKUN LAHU WALIYYUN MENAZ ZULLE\nnor does He need any to protect Him from humiliation,\nوَ كَبِّرْهُ تَكْبِيْرًا\nWA KABBIRHO TAKBEERAN\nand magnify Him for His greatness and glory.\nYou may then say the following:\nيَا سَابِغَ النِّعَمِ\nYAA SAABEGHAN NE-A’ME\nO Conferrer of boon amply!\nيَا دَافِعَ النِّقَمِ\nYAA DAAFE-A’N NE-QAME\nO Repeller of troubles!\nيَا بَارِءَ النَّسَمِ\nYAA BAARE-AN NASAME\nO Maker of souls!\nيَا عَلِيَّ الْهِمَمِ\nYAA A’LIYYAL HEMAME\nO Sublime in determinations!\nيَا مُغْشِيَ الظُّلَمِ\nYAA MUGHSHEYAZ ZOLAME\nO Coverer [of daylight] with darkness!\nيَا ذَا الْجُوْدِ وَ الْكَرَمِ\nYAA ZAL JOODE WAL KARAME\nO Lord of magnanimity and nobility!\nيَا كَاشِفَ الضُّرِّ وَ الْاَلَمِ\nYAA KAASHEFAZ ZURRE WAL ALAME\nO Remover of harm and pains!\nيَا مُوْنِسَ الْمُسْتَوْحِشِيْنَ فِي الظُّلَمِ\nYAA MOONESAL MUSTAWHESHEENE FIZ ZOLAME\nO Entertainer of those lonely in darkness!\nيَا عَالِمًا لَا يُعَلَّمُ\nYAA A’ALEMAN LAA YO-A’LLAMO\nO All-knowing Who never needs teaching!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nSend blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad \nوَ افْعَلْ بِيْ مَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ\nWAF A’L BEE MAA ANTA AHLOHU\nand do to me all that which befits You.\nيَا مَنِ اسْمُهٗ دَوَاۤءٌ\nYAA MANIS MOHU DAWAAA-UN\nO He Whose Name is remedy,\nوَ ذِكْرُهٗ شِفَاۤءٌ\nWA  ZIKROHU SHEFAAA-UN\nthe remembrance of Whom is cure,\nوَ طَاعَتُهٗ غَنَاۤءٌ\nWA TAA-A’TOHU GHANAAA-UN\nand the obedience to Whom is sufficiency,\nاِرْحَمْ مَنْ رَأْسُ مَالِهِ الرَّجَاۤءُ\nIRHAM MAN RAASO MAALEHIR RAJAAA-O\nhave mercy upon him whose wealth is only hope [for You]\nوَ سِلَاحُهُ الْبُكَاۤءُ\nWA SELAAHOHUL BOKAAA-O\nand whose weapon is only weeping.\nسُبْحَانَكَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nSUBHAANAKA LAAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANTA\nGlory be to You. There is no god save You.\nيَا حَنَّانُ يَا مَنَّانُ\nYAA HANNAANO YAA MANNAANO\nO All-tender, O All-Bestower,\nيَا بَدِيْعَ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَ الْاَرْضِ\nYAA BADEE-U’S SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE\nO Fashioner of the heavens and the earth,\nيَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَ الْاِكْرَامِ.\nYAA ZAL JALAALE WAL IKRAAME.\nO Lord of majesty and honor.\nTwenty-Second: It is recommended to recite [Surah al-Jumu’ah](A66) (No. 62) and [Surah al-Munafiqun](A67) (No. 63) in the Zohr (noon) Prayer on Fridays and to recite [Surah al-Jumu’ah](A66) and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) in the Asr (afternoon) Prayer.\nShaykh al-Saduq has narrated that Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq(a.s.) said: It is obligatory upon all believers who claim being adherents (Shi’ah) to us (i.e. to the Ahl al-Bayt) to recite [Surah al-Jumu’ah](A66) and Surah al-A’la (No. 78) in the obligatory prayers at Friday nights and to recite [Surah al-Jumu’ah](A66) and [Surah al-Munafiqun](A67) in the Zohr Prayer on Fridays. One who does so will be regarded as following the example of the Holy Messenger, peace be upon him and his Household, and Almighty Allah will award him Paradise.\nShaykh al-Kulayni has narrated in a semi-authentic narration that al-Halabi asked Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) whether one should recite the Zohr Prayer audibly on Fridays (in case one cannot attend the congregational Friday Prayer). The Imam (a.s.) answered on the affirmative and confirmed that one should recite [Surah al-Jumu’ah](A66) and al-Munafiqun in the Zohr Prayer on Fridays.\nTwenty-Third: With reference to the post-prayer litanies in general and the supplications to be said after the Friday Zohr Prayer, Shaykh al-Tusi has quoted Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq(a.s.) as saying: Whoever recites on Friday after the concluding part of the Zohr Prayer the following parts of the Holy Qur’an, will be under the divine protection all over the week:\n(1) [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) seven times, (2) [Surah al-Naas](A118) seven times, (3) [Surah al-Falaq](A117) seven times, (4) [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) seven times, (5) [Surah al-Kafirun](A113) seven times, (6) the last two verses of [Surah al-Tawbah](A13) (No. 9), (7) the final verses of [Surah al-Hashr](A63), and (8) the final verses of Surah Aal-e-Imran.\nTwenty-Fourth: Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) is also reported to have said: If one says the following supplicatory prayer after the Fajr Prayer or the Zohr Prayer, no sin will be recorded against him for a whole year:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْ صَلَاتَكَ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A’L SALAATAKA\nO Allah, (please do) let Your blessings\nوَ صَلَاةَ مَلَاۤئِكَتِكَ وَ رُسُلِكَ\nWA SALAATA MALAAA-EKATEKA WA ROSOLEKA\nand the blessings of Your angels and Messengers\nعَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nA’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nbe on Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq(a.s.) is also reported to have said: If one says the following supplicatory prayer after the Fajr Prayer or the Zohr Prayer (on Fridays), he will not die before he catches the age of Imam al-Mahdi, peace be upon him:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَ عَجِّلْ فَرَجَهُمْ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADIN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN WA A’JJIL FARAJAHUM\nO Allah, send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad and hasten their Relief.\nThe earlier supplication also brings about security from misfortunes up to the next Friday if it is repeated three times after the Friday Zohr Prayer.\nIt has been also narrated that one who invokes Almighty Allah’s blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household, peace be upon them, between the two obligatory Zohr and Asr prayers will have the reward of offering a seventy-unit prayer.\nTwenty-Fifth: It is recommended to say the following two supplications of al-Sahifah al-Sajjadiyyah al-Kamilah:\n1) Dua No. 46\n2) Dua No.48 \nThen, supplicate as seems proper to you and invoke blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household one thousand times. Thus was Imam Zayn al-’Abidin (a.s.) used to do.\nTwenty-Sixth: In his book of Misbah al-Mutahajjid, Shaykh al-Tusi says that the Holy Imams, peace be upon them, are reported to have said: When one offers, after the obligatory Zohr Prayer on Fridays, a two-unit prayer reciting in each unit [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and repeating [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) seven times and after accomplishment says the following supplicatory prayer, one will be saved against all misfortunes and seditious matters up to the next Friday, and will be joined with Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him and his Household, and Prophet Abraham, peace be upon him:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْنِيْ مِنْ اَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A’LNEE MIN AHLIL JANNATIL\nO Allah, include me with the inhabitants of Paradise\nالَّتِيْ حَشْوُهَا الْبَرَكَةُ\nLATEE HASHWOHAL BARAKATO\nwhose stuffing is blessing\nوَ عُمَّارُهَا الْمَلَاۤئِكَةُ\nWA U’MMAAROHAL MALAAA-EKATO\nand whose constructors are the angels\nمَعَ نَبِيِّنَا مُحَمَّدٍ\nMA-A’ NABIYYENA MOHAMMADIN\nwith our Prophet Muhammad,\nصَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ اٰلِهٖ\nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI\npeace of Allah be upon him and his Household,\nوَ اَبِيْنَا اِبْرَاهِيْمَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ\nWA ABEENAA IBRAAHEEMA A’LAYHIS SALAAMO\nand our father Abraham, peace be upon him.\nCommenting on this supplication, Shaykh al-Tusi instructs that one who is not from the Holy Prophet’s offspring should say, “his father (abihi)” instead of “our father (abina).”"
}
